{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nThe completed Gerrit Verified latency RCA optimized the macOS completion path, but Ubuntu jobs still occupy scarce org-wide runners for 11-14 minutes and contribute to queue contention. Follow-up questions identify three candidate levers: replace repeated Pandoc corpus rendering with static expected results plus a smaller boundary test, remove redundant work from the exhaustive 1,440-minute bridge cadence proof, and move genuinely live Jira DC coverage out of the per-change hot path while retaining fast unit coverage. This work must preserve behavioral coverage and must not use extra parallel jobs or unchanged aggregate runner usage.\n\n## Plan\n- Build a dated Ubuntu runner-time dossier from final post-remediation run 31752047186, pytest duration logs, workflow routing, and focused local runtime experiments.\n- For Pandoc and render_unit, map every current assertion to the code boundary it exercises; compare static golden fixtures, a bounded real-Pandoc contract sample, and full-corpus external execution using defect-seeded experiments to detect any coverage loss. Treat the pinned Pandoc-version-to-output coupling as an explicit external boundary. Any accepted golden fixture must identify its Pandoc version and provide a documented regeneration command.\n- For the bridge cadence test, discriminate between the cost of the 1,440 arithmetic checks and invariant workflow YAML I/O; prefer hoisting invariant I/O if it preserves the exhaustive proof.\n- Inventory expensive Jira DC/default-tier tests, identify which require a real Jira or external binary, and map them to faster existing or new unit contracts before proposing any lane move.\n- Compare each candidate with current practice in at least three named, popular, actively maintained OSS projects. Consensus means at least two-thirds of the surveyed projects, rounded up, use the practice and no surveyed project documents rejecting it for coverage or reliability; otherwise route the proposal to operator disposition.\n- Search tracker history for prior acceptance or rejection of every proposal.\n- Record a confirmed RCA and measured runner-time/wall-time savings. Create linked implementation tickets only for remediations that preserve coverage; under the operator standing approval, implement those meeting the defined OSS-consensus bar through Gerrit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every Ubuntu operation or test phase over 30 seconds in the final sample is attributed to a specific mechanism and measured with a focused baseline.\n- [ ] The Pandoc corpus proposal has an assertion-level coverage map and A/B runtime estimate.\n- [ ] The render_unit proposal has an assertion-level coverage map and A/B runtime estimate.\n- [ ] The bridge-cadence proposal has an assertion-level coverage map and A/B runtime estimate.\n- [ ] The Jira DC lane-move proposal has an assertion-level coverage map and A/B runtime estimate.\n- [ ] Each proposal cites tracker history.\n- [ ] Each proposal cites at least three named popular actively maintained OSS projects and applies the defined consensus rule.\n- [ ] No accepted remediation removes an assertion, behavioral equivalence class, OS/Python cell, or external boundary.\n- [ ] Every moved coverage boundary has an explicit destination and schedule.\n- [ ] Runner-minute savings are quantified without counting parallel matrix time as critical-path wall time.\n- [ ] Expected queue-pressure savings are quantified separately from deterministic execution savings.\n- [ ] Every consensus-backed remediation is implemented on a linked ticket.\n- [ ] Every implemented remediation passes repository gates and Gerrit LLM-Review +1 plus Verified +1 before merge.\n- [ ] Every implemented remediation merges before this task closes.\n- [ ] Non-consensus or coverage-risking proposals are summarized with evidence and left for operator disposition."}},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786668285831388001,"uuid":"acbc0895-eaa8-4500-8244-6c43ba4bebdd"}